# Cloudflare Pages edge headers for the public site.
#
# SYNTAX. Pages reads this file from the root of the served directory (`apps/site`). A rule is a
# path pattern on its own line followed by indented `Name: value` lines; a line beginning with `#`
# is a comment. Cloudflare documents comments only at column 0 and says nothing about indented
# ones, so every comment here sits at column 0 and the rule block below contains header lines and
# nothing else. Limits: 100 rules, 2,000 characters per line.
#
# WHY THE POLICY BELOW IS SHAPED THE WAY IT IS. `apps/site/test/site.test.mjs` asserts that this
# site makes no external request: no `<script>` tag, no `fonts.googleapis.com`, no
# `fonts.gstatic.com`, and `github.com` as the only permitted remote host. That test reads the
# SOURCE. It proves the six files in the repository are clean; it cannot prove the bytes a visitor
# receives are. The Content-Security-Policy below is the same claim expressed as something the
# browser enforces, so the property survives an injected tag, a compromised build, or an edit that
# reaches production without the test running.
#
# The policy was derived from an audit of what these pages actually load, not copied from a
# template:
#   - 12 `<link rel="stylesheet">` (two stylesheets across six pages) are the only subresources.
#   - zero `<script>` tags, zero `style="..."` attributes, zero `<style>` blocks.
#   - zero `<img>`, `<svg>`, `<iframe>`, `<form>`, `<video>`, `<object>`.
#   - zero `url()` in either stylesheet, zero `data:` URIs anywhere.
#   - one off-site URL in the whole site: the `<a href>` to the project repository on github.com,
#     which is a top-level navigation and is not governed by CSP at all.
# The favicon is the only addition to that list, and a favicon is fetched under `img-src`.
#
# DIRECTIVE BY DIRECTIVE.
#
# default-src 'none'
#   The deny-by-default floor. Every fetch directive not named below inherits it, so script-src,
#   font-src, connect-src, frame-src, object-src, media-src, manifest-src and worker-src are all
#   'none' without being spelled out. This is the directive that makes "no external requests" a
#   browser-enforced property rather than a source-code convention. A `<script>` tag added to any
#   page does not run and a webfont added to either stylesheet does not load; the browser console
#   names the blocked directive in both cases, so neither failure is silent.
#
# style-src 'self'
#   assets/tokens.css and assets/site.css, same-origin. Deliberately no 'unsafe-inline': the pages
#   carry no `<style>` block and no `style=` attribute, so an injected one is refused.
#
# img-src 'self'
#   favicon.svg and favicon.ico. The pages reference no other image, and none may be added from a
#   remote host.
#
# base-uri 'none'
#   Every link on this site is relative. An injected `<base href="https://evil.example/">` would
#   silently repoint all of them without needing a line of JavaScript; this refuses it.
#
# form-action 'none'
#   There is no form on this site and no place to submit one. If HTML injection ever puts a form
#   here -- a credential prompt on a page carrying the protocol's own disclaimers is the obvious
#   abuse -- it has nowhere to POST to.
#
# frame-ancestors 'none'
#   Nobody may frame these pages. The material value is not clickjacking, since there is nothing to
#   click, but framing: the pre-launch banner and the not-an-offer disclaimer are load-bearing
#   legal text, and a hostile page that frames this site with the banner cropped out has published
#   the protocol's own words without its disclosures.
#
# X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
#   This origin serves .html, .css, .txt, .xml, .svg and .ico. Content sniffing is the mechanism by
#   which a file served as one type is interpreted as another; nosniff makes the declared
#   Content-Type binding.
#
# Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
#   The only off-site link is the project repository. Without this, following it tells github.com
#   which page a visitor was reading, and /risks or /operators is a meaningful signal about a
#   reader that this site has no reason to disclose. Nothing here wants a referrer -- there is no
#   analytics -- so the strictest value costs nothing.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

# DELIBERATELY ABSENT. Each of these is a standard header that would do nothing on this site, and a
# header that does nothing is a claim of protection the next reader has to disprove:
#
#   X-Frame-Options   -- superseded by frame-ancestors in every browser that ships CSP Level 2.
#   Permissions-Policy -- gates browser APIs that only script can call, and default-src 'none'
#                        means no script can run.
#   Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy, Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy -- protect a JavaScript execution
#                        context and a cross-origin isolation guarantee, neither of which exists.
#   X-XSS-Protection  -- removed from every current browser; its legacy auditor introduced
#                        vulnerabilities of its own.
#
# STRICT-TRANSPORT-SECURITY IS THE OWNER'S DECISION, NOT THIS FILE'S, so it is left commented out.
# HSTS is close to irreversible: once a browser has seen the header it refuses plain HTTP for the
# stated max-age no matter what the server later sends, and `preload` is a registry entry whose
# removal process is measured in months. Cloudflare Pages already serves HTTPS and redirects HTTP,
# so the residual attack this closes is narrow -- an active network attacker stripping TLS on a
# visitor's FIRST navigation to the domain.
#
# The recommended ramp, if the owner wants it. Check Cloudflare SSL/TLS -> Edge Certificates first,
# because the zone may already set HSTS and two sources will disagree:
#   1. max-age=86400     -- one day, fully recoverable within a day
#   2. max-age=31536000  -- one year, apex only
#   3. add includeSubDomains only once every intended subdomain of rwally.com is HTTPS-only
#   4. add preload only as a deliberate decision to accept the removal process
#
# Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=86400
